\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 ==>Terraform is an open-source platform that enables you to define and provision infrastructure as code (IaC) across multiple cloud and on-premises environments.\
\
==>
\f1\b \strokec2 Terraform provides a universal approach to infrastructure automation
\f0\b0 \strokec2  because it supports multiple cloud providers (like AWS, Azure, and GCP) as well as on-premises environments using the same language and workflow.\
\
==>Terraform uses HashiCorp Configuration Language (HCL) to define infrastructure as code.\
\
==>
\f1\b \strokec2 HCL (HashiCorp Configuration Language)
\f0\b0 \strokec2  is used in Terraform to define the desired infrastructure.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 Terraform then uses 
\f1\b \strokec2 cloud provider APIs
\f0\b0 \strokec2  (like AWS, Azure, or GCP APIs) to 
\f1\b \strokec2 communicate with and provision resources
\f0\b0 \strokec2  according to those HCL definitions.\
\
